From 5a24728280a44e484e3fb87662a023edcc252320 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 22:47:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 50/50] pf: unshare the mbuf before hiding SCTP addresses

Between jails on one host the packet travels by reference (epair, bridge)
and its storage can still be shared with data the sender keeps; rewriting
the INIT's address parameters in place changed bytes the peer had signed
into its state cookie, the COOKIE ECHO then failed the HMAC check and
the association never came up. Write into an unshared copy.
---
 sys/netpfil/pf/pf.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sys/netpfil/pf/pf.c b/sys/netpfil/pf/pf.c
index 763862579..0b4f60a09 100644
--- a/sys/netpfil/pf/pf.c
+++ b/sys/netpfil/pf/pf.c
@@ -648,6 +648,23 @@ pf_sctp_hide_addresses(struct pf_pdesc *pd)
 				type = ntohs(h.param_type);
 				if (type == SCTP_IPV4_ADDRESS ||
 				    type == SCTP_IPV6_ADDRESS) {
+					/*
+					 * Write into a private copy: between jails on
+					 * one host the packet is passed by reference
+					 * (epair, bridge), and the storage may still be
+					 * shared with data the sender keeps, e.g. the
+					 * INIT copy a peer signs into its state cookie.
+					 * Rewriting that in place broke the cookie's
+					 * HMAC, and the association never came up.
+					 */
+					if (!changed) {
+						struct mbuf *m;
+
+						m = m_unshare(pd->m, M_NOWAIT);
+						if (m == NULL)
+							return;
+						pd->m = m;
+					}
 					h.param_type = htons(PF_SCTP_HIDDEN_ADDRESS |
 					    (type & 0xff));
 					m_copyback(pd->m, p, sizeof(h.param_type),
